TI  - A 36-Year-Old Male With Left-Sided Neck Pain and Progressive Dyspnea.
PG  - e169-e172
LID - S0012-3692(24)00126-0 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2024.01.034 [doi]
AB  - A 36-year-old male with no significant medical history presented to the ED with 
      progressive left-sided neck and facial pain for the last 7 days. The patient also 
      reported subjective fevers, chills, difficulty opening his mouth, and anorexia 
      for the last 1 week. He denied cough, chest pain or tightness, shortness of 
      breath, skin rashes, dysphagia, or odynophagia. He reported use of two to three 
      59.15 mL beers daily for the last 20 years. There was no recent travel or sick 
      contact exposure. He did not report any TB exposure, IV drug use, or recent 
      sexual encounters.
