TI  - Sepsis in Immunocompromised Host and a Hematologic Complication.
PG  - e47-e55
LID - S0012-3692(23)00358-6 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2023.03.015 [doi]
AB  - A 43-year-old Puerto Rican man with a kidney transplant presented to the ED with 
      2 weeks of flu-like symptoms, nausea, and vomiting. He had plasma exchange 
      therapy 2 months before for acute transplant rejection and has been tolerating a 
      heightened immunosuppressive regimen. CT scans characterized opacities as 
      possibly early tree-in-bud opacities (Fig 1A). Patient remained stable throughout 
      hospital stay with an unremarkable workup and was discharged with doxycycline for 
      nonspecific pneumonia.
