LID - S0012-3692(22)04076-4 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2022.11.008 [doi]
AB  - A 35-year-old man was hospitalized with fever, chest pain, and cough of 2 weeks' 
      duration. These symptoms persisted despite 4 days of antibiotic treatment with IV 
      ceftriaxone sodium 2 g/d. The patient was a nonsmoker with an unremarkable 
      medical history who worked as a herdsman and lived in the Shigate region of 
      Tibet, China.
