TI  - "The report of my death…": Exaggerated Predictions on the Demise of the 
      Stethoscope.
PG  - 872-877
LID - S0012-3692(22)01010-8 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2022.05.016 [doi]
AB  - The narrative of the rise and fall of the stethoscope is partly written. Medical 
      historians agree on the rise in its use; however, on the decline, they are less 
      certain. This article explores the previously unexamined and surprisingly long 
      history of predictions of the stethoscope's demise. It also provides evidence to 
      show that it is not yet extinct, although its applications are changing as it 
      adapts to newer technology and recent public health measures. Primary sources 
      include medical school curricula, books, medical journals, and popular 
      literature. Trends and projections in patent applications for stethoscope 
      modifications and sales of the instrument provide additional evidence for the 
      robust position of the stethoscope in current American practice.
