LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2022.03.052 [doi]
AB  - A 45-year-old man sought treatment at the ED during the third wave of the 
      COVID-19 pandemic with a month-long history of fatigue, cough, myalgia, and hand 
      stiffness. He did not report dyspnea. He had no past medical history and 
      previously was fit and active, working as a farmer. He was a lifelong nonsmoker 
      and had no family history of lung disease.
