TI  - A 63-Year-Old Man With Nonmassive Hemoptysis With a Right Upper Lung Mass.
PG  - e27-e31
LID - S0012-3692(22)00402-0 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2022.02.035 [doi]
AB  - A 63-year-old man, who was a current smoker with a 10-pack-year history, was 
      referred to our hospital for nonmassive hemoptysis for a month, and a large mass 
      was observed in the right upper lobe on chest radiography. He lost 3 kg of weight 
      within a few months. He did not have fever, breathlessness, or night sweats, and 
      he denied a history of liver disease, alcohol consumption, or contact with a 
      person infected with TB. He was previously healthy and was not currently taking 
      any medication.
