TI  - A 31-Year-Old Man With Fever, Atypical Chest Pain, and Mediastinal Mass.
PG  - e299-e304
LID - S0012-3692(21)05216-8 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2021.12.644 [doi]
AB  - A 31-year-old Asian male never-smoker living in the upper Midwest with a past 
      medical history of congenital bilateral hearing loss sought treatment with a 
      1-week history of fever, fatigue, right-sided pleuritic chest pain, shortness of 
      breath, productive cough with mild intermittent hemoptysis, night sweats, and 
      unintentional 10-lb weight loss over 4 weeks. He was adopted from South Korea as 
      an infant, and thus the family history was unknown. He worked in the heating, 
      ventilation, and air conditioning business, performing installations and repairs. 
      There was no known exposure to animals, caves, rivers, lakes, or wooded areas. He 
      travelled to South Korea and New Hampshire approximately 9 months previously. He 
      did not take any medication.
