TI  - Hematology Emergencies in Adults With Critical Illness: Malignant Hematology.
PG  - 120-131
LID - S0012-3692(22)00248-3 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2022.02.004 [doi]
AB  - As outcomes have improved across the hematologic malignancy population, candidacy 
      for ICU admission has increased. This complex population may develop a variety of 
      complications related to their treatment or underlying disease that can result in 
      critical illness necessitating ICU support. This review highlights common causes 
      of critical illness associated with hematologic malignancies, including the 
      following: (1) neutropenic sepsis; (2) hyperleukocytosis and leukostasis across 
      patients with acute myeloid leukemia; (3) complications of acute promyelocytic 
      leukemia; (4) tumor lysis syndrome; and (5) critical care complications that can 
      arise following hematopoietic stem cell transplantation.
