LID - S0012-3692(20)35110-2 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2020.10.057 [doi]
AB  - A 52-year-old man presented with hemoptysis of 2 weeks' duration. He had been 
      experiencing hoarseness, right-sided pleuritic chest pain, subjective fevers, 
      chills, night sweats, and 10 pounds weight loss for the previous 2 months. He 
      additionally reported severe frontal headaches, nasal congestion, and 
      intermittent epistaxis, which had been present for a year before his current 
      presentation. He had worked in construction and denied tobacco or illicit drug 
      use.
