LID - S0012-3692(20)34360-9 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2020.07.096 [doi]
AB  - A 28-year-old man presented with shortness of breath, chest pain, and scant 
      hemoptysis. Three weeks previously, he was admitted for coronavirus disease 2019 
      pneumonia that had been diagnosed by nasal swab polymerase chain reaction. Chest 
      CT imaging demonstrated bilateral ground-glass opacities without evidence of VTE. 
      He was treated with hydroxychloroquine, up to 7 L/min oxygen, and self-proning. 
      After 8 days of hospitalization, he was discharged on 4 L/min oxygen. After 
      discharge, his symptoms and hypoxia resolved.
