TI  - A 6-Year-Old Boy With a Mediastinal Mass.
PG  - e317-e321
LID - S0012-3692(20)31877-8 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2020.07.003 [doi]
AB  - A 6-year-old boy was referred to our hospital with an anterior mediastinal mass. 
      This was discovered by chest radiography performed when the boy was examined 
      after being caught by an elevator door about 2 weeks earlier. The patient had 
      been born full term without any complications during pregnancy or delivery. No 
      clinical symptoms were observed during this presentation, and he had no history 
      of previous infections.
