TI  - A 35-Year-Old Man With Recurrent Pneumonia and Whitish Sputum.
PG  - e229-e232
LID - S0012-3692(20)31719-0 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2020.06.016 [doi]
AB  - A 35-year-old man was admitted for recurrent episodes of pneumonia. He complained 
      of a 2-month history of exertional dyspnea and productive cough with whitish and 
      viscous sputum which was poorly responsive to antibiotic therapy. He also 
      reported a weight loss of 5 kg since the first symptoms appeared. There was no 
      dysphagia, fever, or chest pain. He currently did not use medication and did not 
      have a relevant medical history except a current 10 pack-year smoking history. He 
      did not report any history of trauma or respiratory exposure to fats.
