TI  - Etoposide as Salvage Therapy for Cytokine Storm Due to Coronavirus Disease 2019.
PG  - e7-e11
LID - S0012-3692(20)34486-X [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2020.09.077 [doi]
AB  - Coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-19) has resulted in significant morbidity and 
      mortality because of a lack of effective therapies. Therapeutic strategies under 
      investigation target the overactive cytokine response with anti-cytokine or 
      immunomodulators therapies. We present a unique case of severe cytokine storm 
      resistant to multiple anti-cytokine therapies, but eventually responsive to 
      etoposide. Thus, etoposide may have a role as salvage therapy in treatment of 
      cytokine storm in COVID-19. To our knowledge, this is the first reported case of 
      use of etoposide in COVID-19.
