TI  - A 68-Year-Old Man With Skin Rash and a Pleural Effusion.
PG  - e33-e36
LID - S0012-3692(20)30011-8 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2019.12.013 [doi]
AB  - A 68-year-old man developed an erythematous, papular, pruritic rash on his right 
      thigh 1 month prior to presentation. It subsequently spread to his other 
      extremities and trunk. He also endorsed fevers of > 38.3°C, night sweats, 
      fatigue, shortness of breath, and a dry cough. He was prescribed triamcinolone 
      0.1% cream for his rash and azithromycin for presumed community-acquired 
      pneumonia, with no improvement in symptoms. He had a history of relapsing 
      polychondritis for which he was prescribed infliximab and low-dose prednisone. He 
      had never smoked tobacco, did not use alcohol or illicit substances, and had no 
      significant travel history.
