TI  - A 48-Year-Old South African Woman with Rheumatoid Arthritis and Lung Nodules.
PG  - e151-e155
LID - S0012-3692(19)34294-1 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2019.10.052 [doi]
AB  - We present the case of a 48-year-old South African woman with no smoking history, 
      and seropositive rheumatoid arthritis diagnosed in 2001. She was treated with 
      chloroquine (150 mg, 4 times per week) and methotrexate (30 mg weekly) with 
      well-controlled symptoms until 2015, when she developed a disease flare. Her 
      treatment regimen was changed to leflunomide (20 mg daily) monotherapy with 
      subsequent symptom control. Biologic agents were not accessible because of cost 
      constraints.
