TI  - Unexpected BP Sensitivity to Angiotensin II in a Patient With Coronavirus Disease 
      2019, ARDS, and Septic Shock.
PG  - e55-e58
LID - S0012-3692(20)30747-9 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2020.04.015 [doi]
AB  - We report the case of an 88-year-old man with coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-19) 
      who presented with ARDS and septic shock. The patient had exquisite BP 
      sensitivity to low-dose angiotensin II (Ang-2), allowing for rapid liberation 
      from high-dose vasopressors. We hypothesize that sensitivity to Ang-2 might be 
      related to biological effect of severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 2 
      infection. The case is suggestive of a potential role for synthetic Ang-2 for 
      patients with COVID-19 and septic shock. Further studies are needed to confirm 
      our observed clinical efficacy.
