DP  - 2020 Jul
TI  - Is Mortality a Useful Primary End Point for Critical Care Trials?
PG  - 206-211
LID - S0012-3692(19)34369-7 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2019.11.019 [doi]
AB  - Mortality has long been used as a primary end point for randomized controlled 
      trials in critical care. Recently, a plurality of trials targeting mortality end 
      points as their primary outcome has failed to detect a difference between study 
      arms. While there are a number of reasons for the preponderance of such neutral 
      trials, the use of mortality as an outcome is one important consideration. We 
      explore some of the reasons why such trials may be biased toward a neutral 
      result, as well as reasons to consider alternative end points that are better 
      coupled to the expected therapeutic effect. We also discuss to what extent 
      mortality as a binary outcome is patient-important in the ICU.
