TI  - Potassium Chloride-Induced Phlebitis via a Malpositioned Central Venous Catheter.
PG  - e253-e254
LID - S0012-3692(23)00167-8 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2023.01.035 [doi]
AB  - We present a case of potassium chloride-induced phlebitis with severe, burning, 
      left-sided chest pain when infused via a malpositioned central venous catheter. 
      Using a malpositioned central venous catheter requires careful consideration, but 
      this novel case prompts the need for additional review before its use for the 
      infusion of potentially irritating medications.
