TI  - Value-Based Care for Chest Physicians.
PG  - 1193-1200
LID - S0012-3692(23)00021-1 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2022.12.041 [doi]
AB  - Value-based care aims to improve the health outcomes of patients, eliminate waste 
      and unwarranted clinical variation, and reduce the total cost of care. 
      Professional medical societies have put forward guidelines to raise awareness on 
      unproven practice patterns (Choosing Wisely Campaign), and payers have sought to 
      replace the traditional fee-for-service payment models with value-based contracts 
      that share financial gains or losses based on achieving high-quality outcomes and 
      lowering the cost of care. Regardless of whether their practices are engaged in 
      value-based arrangements, chest physicians should seek understanding of these 
      principles, participate in designing and implementing practical and impactful 
      high-value initiatives in their practices, and have a national voice on the path 
      forward.
