TI  - A 37-Year-Old Woman Presenting With Hemoptysis, Dyspnea and Fever.
PG  - e159-e162
LID - S0012-3692(21)04083-6 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2021.10.002 [doi]
AB  - A 37-year-old woman presented to the ED in Singapore with a 6-month history of 
      chronic cough and dyspnea that was associated with small volume hemoptysis, night 
      sweats and occasional fever. Of note, she had no sick contacts or recent travel. 
      Systemic review revealed no loss of weight or appetite and no autoimmune 
      features. She had no other medical history and was a lifelong nonsmoker and was 
      not an alcoholic.
