TI  - A Rare Cause of Respiratory Insufficiency in a 30-Year-Old Transgender Woman.
PG  - e339-e342
LID - S0012-3692(21)01085-0 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2021.05.054 [doi]
AB  - A 30-year-old transgender woman who was HIV positive presented to the ED with 
      progressive severe dyspnea and hemoptysis that started 1 day earlier. The patient 
      was undergoing antiretroviral therapy with emtricitabine-rilpivirine-tenofovir 
      with good compliance and feminizing hormone therapy with cyproterone acetate. She 
      was otherwise healthy and was not taking any other medications.
