      Hemothorax.
PG  - e243-e246
LID - S0012-3692(20)35093-5 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2020.10.043 [doi]
AB  - A 43-year-old man urgently was referred to the hospital complaining of rapidly 
      worsening dyspnea and right-side chest wall discomfort for 1 hour. Two hours 
      later, he experienced acute respiratory failure that subsequently required 
      intubation and invasive mechanical ventilation, thus he was transferred to ICU. 
      He had no fever, weight loss, or bleeding tendency. He was previously healthy 
      with no history of trauma and was not currently on any medication.
