TI  - A 55-Year-Old Immunocompetent Man With Chest Discomfort and Night Sweats.
PG  - e323-e326
LID - S0012-3692(20)32069-9 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2020.07.045 [doi]
AB  - A 55-year-old Chinese man without significant medical history presented with 
      progressive chest discomfort and night sweats for the past 2 months. He 
      experienced nonexertional chest tightness and palpitation at night, not 
      associated with dyspnea. These symptoms usually lasted for a few minutes and 
      resolved spontaneously. He also reported night sweats but denied fever, chills, 
      or weight change. He had never smoked and denied recent contact with anyone known 
      to be ill.
