TI  - A 52-Year-Old Man Presented With Cough, Chest Pain, and a Mass in the Right Lung.
PG  - e241-e244
LID - S0012-3692(20)31819-5 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2020.06.030 [doi]
AB  - A 52-year-old man, current smoker with a 50 pack-year history, presented to our 
      department with cough, yellow sputum, and localized right chest pain. Chest 
      radiograph revealed a large mass in the right upper lobe. He denied the presence 
      of fever, night sweats, or weight loss. He has a medical history of COPD and 
      anxiety disorder. He was receiving long-acting beta agonists/long-acting 
      muscarinic antagonists as a treatment for COPD and quetiapine 100 mg for anxiety 
      disorder.
