TI  - A 59-Year-Old Man With Chronic Kidney Disease After Kidney Transplantation 
      Presents With Chronic Dyspnea.
PG  - e9-e12
LID - S0012-3692(19)33462-2 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2019.08.1918 [doi]
AB  - A 59-year-old man presented to the ED with a chief complaint of shortness of 
      breath. His past medical history was significant for end-stage renal disease 
      secondary to lithium toxicity, immunosuppression subsequent to cadaveric renal 
      transplantation, bipolar disorder, and hypertension. His shortness of breath had 
      begun 6 months previously and was initially intermittent; it then progressed to 
      constant shortness of breath over the few weeks before presentation. He had no 
      fever, hemoptysis, or chest pain. The patient was admitted to hospital for 
      further evaluation.
