TI  - A 61-Year-Old Man With Shortness of Breath and Eye Swelling.
PG  - e219-e222
LID - S0012-3692(22)04170-8 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2022.11.020 [doi]
AB  - A 61-year-old man presented to the pulmonary clinic with symptoms of dyspnea and 
      productive cough for the last 6 months. Within the last 2 months, he started 
      noticing bulging of his eyes associated with blurry vision. He denied hemoptysis, 
      fever, night sweats, weight loss, skin rash, and dry eyes or mouth. He is a 
      former smoker, and he denied any recent travel history. The patient has a history 
      of microscopic polyangiitis, which was treated with cyclophosphamide and 
      mycophenolate maintenance therapy and has been in remission for the last 7 years.
