TI  - A 33-Year-Old Man With Acute Hemoptysis.
PG  - e13-e18
LID - S0012-3692(22)00883-2 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2022.04.140 [doi]
AB  - A 33-year-old man with a medical history of childhood exercise-induced asthma 
      presented to the ED with 2 days of hemoptysis. He described the hemoptysis as 
      bright red blood with clots, approximately 100 cm(3) in total. He denied prior 
      hemoptysis, pulmonary infections, or exposure to TB. Years ago he had an episode 
      of gross hematuria, but a urologic workup was unrevealing.
