TI  - An Unusual Case of Postpartum Empyema.
PG  - e157-e159
LID - S0012-3692(22)01046-7 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2022.05.019 [doi]
AB  - We present the case of a 32-year-old woman with a left empyema and T12 
      osteomyelitis resulting from group B Streptococcus infection occurring 3 weeks 
      after instrumental delivery of a healthy boy. Empyema is a rare complication of 
      instrumental delivery, and this patient highlights the maternal risk resulting 
      from group B Streptococcus bacteremia.
