TI  - A 35-Year-Old Man With Fever, Cough, and Erythematous-Erosive Mucous Membrane 
      Lesions Accompanied by a Generalized Cutaneous Rash.
PG  - e139-e143
LID - S0012-3692(22)00489-5 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2022.03.022 [doi]
AB  - A 35-year-old man presented to the ED with a 7-day history of fever, asthenia, 
      and cough. He had previously received a 3-day course of amoxicillin and 
      clavulanic acid (1 g tid po) and then ceftriaxone (1 g IM once per day) 
      prescribed by his general practitioner with no substantial benefit. He was an 
      active smoker (11.2 pack/y), without known allergy-related syndromes and any 
      important reports in his medical history.
