TI  - Cavitating Lung Disease Associated With Sudden Death.
PG  - e279-e285
LID - S0012-3692(21)04427-5 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2021.11.025 [doi]
AB  - A 16-year-old boy presented with 6 days of left iliac fossa pain. He had a 
      medical history of right subtalar dislocation and appendicitis requiring 
      laparotomy 3 years earlier, complicated by wound dehiscence. His family history 
      was significant for his brother's sudden death 3 weeks prior after a 12-month 
      illness with intermittent epigastric pain, weight loss, and hemoptysis. Travel 
      history was significant for travel to the Philippines 3 years prior, in which he 
      spent time in the hospital for appendicitis.
