TI  - A Pregnant Woman With Hemoptysis and Diffuse Pulmonary Nodules.
PG  - e651-e656
LID - S0012-3692(21)01392-1 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2021.07.038 [doi]
AB  - A 22-year-old woman who was 36 weeks pregnant presented with a 4-day history of 
      cough, hemoptysis, and exertional dyspnea. She had no fever, night sweats, or 
      weight loss. The review of system was otherwise negative. Her medical history was 
      notable for a spontaneous first-trimester abortion a year ago. At that time, she 
      had a transvaginal ultrasound scan that showed a gestational sac with no fetal 
      movement. A post-abortion ultrasound scan revealed no residual fetal parts.
