TI  - A 58-Year-Old Woman With Lung Nodules and Chronic Cough.
PG  - e285-e288
LID - S0012-3692(21)00859-X [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2021.04.051 [doi]
AB  - A 58-year-old woman was referred to our department with a cough of 1 year 
      duration; her condition was unresponsive to the administration of inhaled steroid 
      and beta-2 agonists. She denied the presence of dyspnea, chest pain, or other 
      extrapulmonary symptoms. She was a never-smoker with a negative medical history 
      and no occupational or domestic exposures. There was no history of cancer, 
      gastroesophageal reflux disease, asthma, allergic rhinitis, or other allergies.
