TI  - A 29-Year-Old Woman With Cough, Dry Eyes, Pulmonary Cysts, and Nodules.
PG  - e195-e198
LID - S0012-3692(21)00451-7 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2021.02.051 [doi]
AB  - A 29-year-old woman who is a never smoker and has a medical history of systemic 
      hypertension presented with a 3-week history of generalized fatigue and dry 
      cough. She endorsed sicca symptoms of dry eyes and dry mouth. She denied 
      breathlessness, fever, chills, night sweats, or weight loss. She had no 
      heartburn, postnasal drip, joint pain, swelling, or skin lesions. She had no 
      known lung disease or history of pneumothorax. Her family history was 
      unremarkable.
