TI  - Rare Diagnosis of a Multilobular Pulmonary Mass.
PG  - e63-e67
LID - S0012-3692(21)00106-9 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2021.01.034 [doi]
AB  - A 57-year-old woman was admitted to our hospital for an abnormal chest shadow 
      found during routine chest radiography. She had no respiratory symptoms. Her 
      medical history included dyslipidemia, and her surgical history included 
      conization for cervical cancer at age 38 years. She was a social drinker and 
      ex-smoker of approximately 10 cigarettes per day (from ages 20 to 30 years); she 
      denied recreational drug use.
