PG  - e395-e401
LID - S0012-3692(21)00052-0 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2021.01.019 [doi]
AB  - A 67-year-old woman, who recently immigrated to the United States from 
      Afghanistan, presented to the hospital after sustaining a mechanical fall. She 
      had no significant medical history and was not on any medication routinely. She 
      denied any fever, night sweats, weight loss, shortness of breath, or hemoptysis. 
      The patient had no prior personal history or exposure to TB. Results of a 
      previous purified protein derivative skin test upon immigration were negative.
