TI  - A 57-Year-Old Man With Stridor and Critical Tracheal Narrowing.
PG  - e385-e388
LID - S0012-3692(21)00029-5 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2021.01.006 [doi]
AB  - A 57-year-old man with a history of polysubstance use presented with shortness of 
      breath, wheezing, productive cough, subjective fever, and chills of 3-day 
      duration. Additionally, he reported worsening shortness of breath for the last 
      3 months. Of note, the patient was reported to have had, in the previous 
      6 months, two episodes of pneumonia that was treated with antibiotics and 
      steroids. He was also diagnosed several years prior with adult-onset asthma due 
      to intermittent wheezing and was prescribed an albuterol inhaler. The albuterol 
      did not help relieve his wheezing, and he stopped refilling it.
