TI  - A 19-Year-Old Pregnant Woman With Pulmonary Hypertension With Progressive 
      Dyspnea.
PG  - e371-e375
LID - S0012-3692(21)00022-2 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2020.12.048 [doi]
AB  - A 19-year-old pregnant woman at week 32 of gestation was referred to our clinic 
      with progressive shortness of breath for the further evaluation and treatment of 
      high-risk pregnancy. Her complaints had been existing since her childhood. Two 
      years prior to her admission, she had been diagnosed with heart failure with 
      preserved ejection fraction due to cardiomyopathy and associated pulmonary 
      hypertension. The patient had no family history of any cardiac disease. She had 
      never smoked or drunk alcohol. Her clinical condition had deteriorated 
      progressively with the pregnancy.
