TI  - Respiratory Distress and Chest Pain in an Airplane Passenger With Radiolucent 
      Left Hemithorax.
PG  - e319-e323
LID - S0012-3692(20)35459-3 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2020.12.014 [doi]
AB  - A 43-year-old man experienced sudden onset of chest pain and shortness of breath 
      onboard a domestic flight. After consultation with the airline's operations 
      center, a decision was made to land the plane in its destination airport. After 
      landing, an ambulance was ready, and the patient was transferred to the ED in our 
      facility. Patient evaluation was immediately started, and oxygen supply and 
      venous access were secured.
