LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2020.09.276 [doi]
AB  - A 14-year old girl presented with history of productive cough since the age of 3 
      years. For the past 6 years, she complained of chest tightness and wheezing. 
      There was also nasal stuffiness and discharge for the past 6 years. She denied 
      history of hemoptysis, ear discharge, or chest pain. There was no history of 
      respiratory distress at the time of birth. Her brother also suffered from 
      productive cough and wheezing since the age of 3 years. However, both her parents 
      were asymptomatic.
