TI  - A 29-Year-Old Man With an Osteolytic Rib Lesion.
PG  - e115-e117
LID - S0012-3692(20)34509-8 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2020.09.089 [doi]
AB  - A 29-year-old man with no significant medical history presented to the ED with a 
      4-week history of chest pain. The pain was insidious, located on the right side 
      of the chest, increased by deep breathing, and incompletely alleviated by 
      acetaminophen. The patient had never smoked tobacco. He denied any recent fevers, 
      chills, dyspnea, cough, night sweats, hemoptysis, or history of trauma but had 
      lost at least 8 kg in the past 6 months. The patient was from Morocco and had 
      lived in France for 1 year.
