TI  - Unexplained Hypoxemia in a Patient With Transient Ischemic Attack.
PG  - e19-e22
LID - S0012-3692(21)01501-4 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2021.07.050 [doi]
AB  - An 84-year-old woman with a medical history of hypertension, hypothyroidism, and 
      transient ischemic attacks presented with right-sided upper and lower extremity 
      weakness for 1 day. She was a lifetime nonsmoker with no known heart disease or 
      chronic lung disease. She had no occupational exposure or pertinent family 
      history. She denied any fevers, chills, rashes, or shortness of breath. There was 
      no history of recent travel.
