LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2021.07.029 [doi]
AB  - A 17-year-old previously healthy Taiwanese girl presented with syncope on a 
      background of 1 month of weakness, polyarthritis, and heliotrope rash. Her 
      presentation and investigations, which included an elevated creatine 
      phosphokinase level and diffuse myositis on lower limb MRI, were consistent with 
      juvenile dermatomyositis (JDM).
