TI  - Mold in Foam Pillows and Mattresses: A Novel Cause of Hypersensitivity 
      Pneumonitis.
PG  - e259-e263
LID - S0012-3692(21)00896-5 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2021.04.068 [doi]
AB  - Hypersensitivity pneumonitis (HP) is an inflammatory and/or fibrotic disease 
      affecting the lung parenchyma and small airways. It typically results from an 
      immune-mediated reaction provoked by an overt or occult inhaled antigen in 
      susceptible individuals. The chronic or fibrotic form of HP has a poor prognosis, 
      especially when no inciting antigen is identified, which occurs in up to 60% of 
      cases. We report two cases of HP associated with exposure to mold in foam pillows 
      and a mattress, which has not previously been reported as a risk factor for HP. 
      Given the high prevalence of foam in pillows and mattresses, mold in foam in 
      bedding may explain many HP cases with a previously unrecognized cause. Early 
      identification and avoidance of foam in bedding may prevent HP progression to 
      end-stage pulmonary fibrosis and death.
