TI  - Histopathological Correlation of Acute on Chronic Eosinophilic Pneumonitis Caused 
      by Vaporized Cannabis Oil Inhalation.
PG  - e137-e139
LID - S0012-3692(20)34908-4 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2020.10.016 [doi]
AB  - Whether eosinophilic pneumonitis represents a true manifestation of e-cigarette, 
      or vaping, product use-associated lung injury remains uncertain, and this 
      ambiguity stems from a lack of histopathological data. We present a previously 
      healthy young woman whose asthma-like symptoms and histopathologic finding of 
      eosinophilic pneumonitis were caused by inhalation of vaporized cannabis hash oil 
      concentrates. This report provides compelling evidence that eosinophilic 
      pneumonitis can result from cannabis hash oil inhalation.
