TI  - Pulmonary Manifestations of Torture.
PG  - 2384-2391
LID - S0012-3692(21)00270-1 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2021.02.010 [doi]
AB  - Despite international treaties banning torture, it is still widely practiced by 
      state agents and private citizens alike. Pulmonologists may encounter survivors 
      of torture in routine clinical practice or in the context of a forensic medical 
      evaluation. The Istanbul Protocol delineates the general approach to the 
      effective medical examination, investigation, and reporting of an individual 
      alleging torture, but relatively little text is devoted to the specific pulmonary 
      manifestations of torture. This review intends to address this paucity.
