TI  - Lung Ultrasound for Patients With Coronavirus Disease 2019 Pulmonary Disease.
PG  - 205-211
LID - S0012-3692(20)34275-6 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2020.08.2054 [doi]
AB  - Given the general utility of lung ultrasound for the evaluation of respiratory 
      failure in acutely ill patients, it is logical to consider its specific 
      advantages in coronavirus disease 2019-related pulmonary disease. The authors, 
      representing the extensive experience of the North American and European 
      coronavirus disease 2019 epicenters, present an ultrasound scanning protocol and 
      report on the common associated ultrasound findings.
