LID - S0012-3692(19)34206-0 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2019.10.038 [doi]
AB  - A 36-year-old woman with a history of hypertension and alcoholism reported 2 days 
      of left upper quadrant pain and jaundice. Within hours of admission, she became 
      somnolent and hypoxic. The patient was then intubated. She had no history of drug 
      abuse, cigarette smoking, liver disease, autoimmune disease, or pancreatitis. She 
      had no home medications.
